# BuildConfig → Shipwright Conversion — `rfipconfig-be` Runtime Image

Converts the legacy chained BuildConfig pair into two Shipwright Builds. The
S2I (builder) Build already works; this adds the **runtime Build** that
produces the final deployable `rfipconfig-be` image.

Placeholder convention: every value that must not be hardcoded is marked
**`<need to be filled - description>`** in the files.

---

## 1. Conversion mechanism — element-by-element mapping

Legacy BuildConfig #2 (`rfipconfig-be-#{JENKINS_TAG}#`, Docker strategy) → Shipwright:

| Legacy element | Legacy value | Shipwright equivalent | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| `source.dockerfile` (inline) | 14-line inline dockerfile | Real `Dockerfile` in Git | `Dockerfile` (repo, Step 1) |
| `source.images` (chained image input) | `from: rfipconfig-be-builder:#{IMAGE_TAG}#`, `paths: /opt/app-root/ → .` | Multi-stage build: `ARG BUILDER_IMAGE` + `FROM ${BUILDER_IMAGE} AS builder` + `COPY --from=builder /opt/app-root/app.tar.gz .` | `Dockerfile` + `paramValues.builder-image` |
| Inline base64 entrypoint (`RUN echo -n '<b64>' \| base64 -d`) | decoded to `/tmp/entrypoint.sh` | Real `entrypoint.sh` in Git + `COPY entrypoint.sh /tmp/entrypoint.sh` | `entrypoint.sh` (repo, Step 1) |
| `RUN yum install unixODBC` / `RUN curl … ibm-iaccess … rpm -i` | package installs at build time | **Intentionally omitted for this case** (per decision). If ever needed again, they belong in the base image, not the app build | — |
| `strategy.dockerStrategy.noCache: true` | | `--no-cache` flag (strategy param `no-cache`, default `true`) | `buildah-hl.yaml` |
| `strategy.dockerStrategy.forcePull: true` | | `--pull=always` flag (strategy param `force-pull`, default `true`) | `buildah-hl.yaml` |
| `strategy.dockerStrategy.imageOptimizationPolicy: SkipLayers` | | No direct equivalent; nearest is buildah `--squash` (not enabled — evaluate later) | — |
| `output.to ImageStreamTag rfipconfig-be:#{IMAGE_TAG}#` | | `output.image: image-registry…/openshift-builds/rfipconfig-be:<tag>` — pushing to the internal registry creates the imagestreamtag automatically; no ImageStream object needed | `rfipconfig-be.yaml` |
| `sourceSecret` (ssh-auth) | `github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-…` | `source.git.cloneSecret` (already exists in `secret.yaml`) | `rfipconfig-be.yaml` |
| `triggers: ConfigChange / ImageChange` | | **No Shipwright equivalent.** Manual `BuildRun` for the PoC; Tekton Triggers + Pipeline chaining replace this in the pipeline task | `buildrun-runtime.yaml` |
| `runPolicy: Serial`, build history limits | | Sequential BuildRuns are the pipeline's job; retention via `BuildRun.spec.retention` (deferred) | — |
| `#{JENKINS_TAG}#` name suffixes | Jenkins templating | `<need to be filled>` markers; parameterization moves to the pipeline task | all files |
| ImageStream objects (2) | | Not needed (see output row) | — |

**How the chained build works now:** the S2I Build (with `DOTNET_PACK=true`)
produces `/opt/app-root/app.tar.gz` inside the builder image and pushes it as
`rfipconfig-be-builder:<tag>`. The runtime Build passes that image reference as
`--build-arg BUILDER_IMAGE=…`; buildah pulls it as stage 1 (same registry
auth/TLS path as the already-working push), copies out `app.tar.gz`, and layers
it onto the clean `hl-dotnet` base — same result as the legacy
`source.images` + `COPY app-root/app.tar.gz .`, but standard Dockerfile
mechanics with no OpenShift-specific image-input machinery.

