## 3. Build order & instructions

### Step 1 — Commit runtime files to Git
```bash
mkdir -p <need to be filled - e.g. runtime/>
cp Dockerfile entrypoint.sh <runtime-dir>/
git add <runtime-dir>/ && git commit -m "Runtime image: Dockerfile + extracted entrypoint" && git push
```
`entrypoint.sh` needs these env vars **at deploy time** (Deployment, not build):
`AUTH_PASSWORD`, `APP_DLL`, `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT` — plus the pfx mounted at
`/etc/pki/tls/private/auth-clientSecrets.pfx`.

### Step 2 — Apply the strategy (cluster-admin)
```bash
oc apply -f buildah-hl.yaml
oc get clusterbuildstrategy buildah-hl
```

### Step 3 — Apply both Builds
```bash
oc apply -f rfipconfig-be.yaml
oc get builds.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds   # both must show Succeeded (registered)
```

### Step 4 — Re-run the S2I BuildRun (new output name)
```bash
oc create -f buidlrun.yaml      # existing S2I buildrun
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds -w
# wait for SUCCEEDED=True, confirm:
oc get istag -n openshift-builds | grep rfipconfig-be-builder
```

### Step 5 — Run the runtime BuildRun
```bash
oc create -f buildrun-runtime.yaml     # create, NOT apply (generateName)
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds -w
oc logs -f <pod> -n openshift-builds --all-containers
```

### Step 6 — Verify
- [ ] Stage-1 pull of `rfipconfig-be-builder` from internal registry OK (no x509 / auth error)
- [ ] Base pull from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` OK (no x509)
- [ ] Push OK, BuildRun `SUCCEEDED=True`
- [ ] `oc get istag -n openshift-builds | grep 'rfipconfig-be:'` shows the final image
- [ ] Smoke test: `oc run` / deploy the image; container starts `/tmp/entrypoint.sh` (needs the 3 env vars + pfx mount)
- [ ] CLI only — console BuildRun page still crashes (OCPBUGS-84214, v1.8.1)

Dependency/pre-flight checks, field contracts, and the troubleshooting table
are unchanged from the previous README revision — they all still apply
(`builds.shipwright.io` qualification, dockerconfigjson secret type, CA
configMap resolution in the BuildRun namespace, etc.).

